<!DOCTYPE html>

<html lang="en">
<head>
 <meta charset="UTF-8">
 <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">

 <title>ITCode - Programming Tutorials</title>
 <meta name="description" content="ITCode — Learn to Code">

 <style>
 * {
 box-sizing: border-box;
 }

 html {
 scroll-behavior: smooth;
 }

 body {
 margin: 0;
 background: #f7f7f5;
 color: #222;
 font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
 line-height: 1.6;
 }

 a {
 color: inherit;
 text-decoration: none;
 }

 /* Header */

 header {
 height: 62px;
 background: #fff;
 border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd;
 display: flex;
 align-items: center;
 padding: 0 32px;
 }

 .header-inner {
 width: 100%;
 max-width: 1100px;
 margin: auto;
 display: flex;
 align-items: center;
 justify-content: space-between;
 }

 .logo {
 font-size: 21px;
 font-weight: bold;
 letter-spacing: -0.5px;
 }

 .logo span {
 color: #2864d7;
 }

 nav {
 display: flex;
 gap: 24px;
 font-size: 14px;
 color: #555;
 }

 nav a:hover {
 color: #111;
 }

 /* Main */

 main {
 max-width: 1100px;
 margin: auto;
 padding: 55px 25px 80px;
 }

 .intro {
 max-width: 720px;
 margin-bottom: 65px;
 }

 .intro h1 {
 margin: 0 0 15px;
 font-size: 42px;
 line-height: 1.15;
 letter-spacing: -1.5px;
 font-weight: 700;
 }

 .intro p {
 margin: 0;
 max-width: 650px;
 color: #666;
 font-size: 17px;
 }

 /* Section */

 section {
 margin-bottom: 65px;
 }

 .section-title {
 margin-bottom: 22px;
 padding-bottom: 10px;
 border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd;
 }

 .section-title h2 {
 display: inline;
 margin: 0;
 font-size: 25px;
 letter-spacing: -0.5px;
 }

 .section-title p {
 display: inline;
 margin-left: 12px;
 color: #888;
 font-size: 14px;
 }

 /* Tutorials */

 .tutorials {
 display: grid;
 grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
 gap: 14px;
 }

 .tutorial {
 background: white;
 border: 1px solid #ddd;
 padding: 23px;
 transition: border-color 0.15s, transform 0.15s;
 }

 .tutorial:hover {
 border-color: #aaa;
 transform: translateY(-2px);
 }

 .tutorial h3 {
 margin: 0 0 7px;
 font-size: 19px;
 }

 .tutorial p {
 margin: 0 0 14px;
 color: #666;
 font-size: 14px;
 max-width: 500px;
 }

 .read {
 color: #2864d7;
 font-size: 13px;
 font-weight: bold;
 }

 /* Small category label */

 .label {
 display: block;
 margin-bottom: 8px;
 color: #888;
 font-size: 11px;
 text-transform: uppercase;
 letter-spacing: 0.7px;
 }

 /* Featured */

 .featured {
 background: #20252b;
 color: white;
 padding: 30px;
 margin-bottom: 65px;
 }

 .featured .label {
 color: #aeb6c0;
 }

 .featured h2 {
 margin: 0 0 8px;
 font-size: 27px;
 }

 .featured p {
 margin: 0 0 18px;
 color: #c4c9cf;
 max-width: 650px;
 }

 .featured a {
 display: inline-block;
 padding: 9px 15px;
 background: white;
 color: #20252b;
 font-size: 13px;
 font-weight: bold;
 }

 /* Networking list */

 .network-list {
 background: white;
 border: 1px solid #ddd;
 }

 .network-item {
 display: flex;
 align-items: center;
 justify-content: space-between;
 padding: 17px 20px;
 border-bottom: 1px solid #e5e5e5;
 }

 .network-item:last-child {
 border-bottom: none;
 }

 .network-item:hover {
 background: #fafafa;
 }

 .network-name {
 font-weight: bold;
 }

 .network-description {
 color: #777;
 font-size: 13px;
 margin-top: 2px;
 }

 .arrow {
 color: #2864d7;
 font-size: 18px;
 }

 /* Quick links */

 .quick-links {
 display: flex;
 flex-wrap: wrap;
 gap: 9px;
 }

 .quick-links a {
 background: white;
 border: 1px solid #d8d8d8;
 padding: 9px 14px;
 font-size: 13px;
 color: #444;
 }

 .quick-links a:hover {
 border-color: #aaa;
 color: #111;
 }

 /* Footer */

 footer {
 border-top: 1px solid #ddd;
 background: white;
 padding: 28px 25px;
 color: #777;
 font-size: 13px;
 }

 .footer-inner {
 max-width: 1100px;
 margin: auto;
 display: flex;
 justify-content: space-between;
 }

 /* Mobile */

 @media (max-width: 700px) {
 header {
 padding: 0 18px;
 }

 nav {
 display: none;
 }

 main {
 padding: 40px 18px 60px;
 }

 .intro h1 {
 font-size: 34px;
 }

 .tutorials {
 grid-template-columns: 1fr;
 }

 .section-title p {
 display: block;
 margin: 3px 0 0;
 }

 .network-item {
 gap: 15px;
 }

 .footer-inner {
 flex-direction: column;
 gap: 5px;
 }
 }
 </style>

</head>

<body>

<header>
 <div class="header-inner">


<a href="#/index.html" class="logo">
 <span>IT</span>Code
</a>

<nav>
 <a href="#/index.html">Home</a>
 <a href="#programming">Programming</a>
 <a href="#networking">Networking</a>
 <a href="#other">Other</a>
</nav>


 </div>
</header>

<main>

 <div class="intro">
 <h1>ITCode</h1>


<p>
 Tutorials about programming, web development, networking, and
 the stuff that makes the internet work. Nothing too complicated —
 just explanations and examples you can actually follow.
</p>


 </div>

 <div class="featured">
 <span class="label">Start here</span>


<h2>How does the web actually work?</h2>

<p>
 When you type a website into your browser, quite a lot happens
 before the page appears. Learn about DNS, TCP, HTTP, TLS, and
 how your browser talks to a server.
</p>

<a href="/study/http">Read the HTTP tutorial →</a>


 </div>

 <section id="programming">


<div class="section-title">
 <h2>Programming</h2>
 <p>Learn the basics and build things.</p>
</div>

<div class="tutorials">

 <a href="/study/python" class="tutorial">
 <span class="label">Programming</span>
 <h3>Python</h3>
 <p>
 A beginner-friendly introduction to Python. Variables,
 conditions, loops, functions, lists, files, and more.
 </p>
 <span class="read">Read tutorial →</span>
 </a>

 <a href="/study/node" class="tutorial">
 <span class="label">JavaScript</span>
 <h3>Node.js</h3>
 <p>
 Learn how JavaScript can run outside the browser. We'll
 cover npm, modules, servers, files, and APIs.
 </p>
 <span class="read">Read tutorial →</span>
 </a>

 <a href="/study/javascript" class="tutorial">
 <span class="label">Web</span>
 <h3>JavaScript</h3>
 <p>
 Start with the language behind interactive websites and
 work your way up to the DOM, events, promises, and APIs.
 </p>
 <span class="read">Read tutorial →</span>
 </a>

 <a href="/study/html" class="tutorial">
 <span class="label">Web</span>
 <h3>HTML & CSS</h3>
 <p>
 Learn how webpages are put together, from basic HTML
 elements to layouts and responsive CSS.
 </p>
 <span class="read">Read tutorial →</span>
 </a>

 <a href="/study/git" class="tutorial">
 <span class="label">Tools</span>
 <h3>Git</h3>
 <p>
 Commits, branches, repositories, remotes, and the commands
 you'll use when working on a project.
 </p>
 <span class="read">Read tutorial →</span>
 </a>

 <a href="/study/apis" class="tutorial">
 <span class="label">Web</span>
 <h3>APIs</h3>
 <p>
 What an API is, how requests and responses work, JSON,
 endpoints, and how to make your own.
 </p>
 <span class="read">Read tutorial →</span>
 </a>

</div>


 </section>

 <section id="networking">


<div class="section-title">
 <h2>Networking</h2>
 <p>What's happening underneath the browser?</p>
</div>

<div class="network-list">

 <a href="/study/tcp" class="network-item">
 <div>
 <div class="network-name">TCP/IP</div>
 <div class="network-description">
 Packets, IP addresses, ports, connections, and routing.
 </div>
 </div>

 <div class="arrow">→</div>
 </a>

 <a href="/study/http" class="network-item">
 <div>
 <div class="network-name">HTTP</div>
 <div class="network-description">
 Requests, responses, headers, status codes, and methods.
 </div>
 </div>

 <div class="arrow">→</div>
 </a>

 <a href="/study/dns" class="network-item">
 <div>
 <div class="network-name">DNS</div>
 <div class="network-description">
 How a domain name eventually turns into an IP address.
 </div>
 </div>

 <div class="arrow">→</div>
 </a>

 <a href="/study/tls" class="network-item">
 <div>
 <div class="network-name">TLS / HTTPS</div>
 <div class="network-description">
 Encryption, certificates, and secure connections.
 </div>
 </div>

 <div class="arrow">→</div>
 </a>

 <a href="/study/websockets" class="network-item">
 <div>
 <div class="network-name">WebSockets</div>
 <div class="network-description">
 Keeping a connection open for real-time communication.
 </div>
 </div>

 <div class="arrow">→</div>
 </a>

</div>


 </section>

 <section id="other">


<div class="section-title">
 <h2>Other stuff</h2>
 <p>A few more things worth knowing.</p>
</div>

<div class="quick-links">
 <a href="/study/linux">Linux</a>
 <a href="/study/cli">Command Line</a>
 <a href="/study/databases">Databases</a>
 <a href="/study/sql">SQL</a>
 <a href="/study/json">JSON</a>
 <a href="/study/ssh">SSH</a>
 <a href="/study/security">Web Security</a>
 <a href="/study/servers">Web Servers</a>
 <a href="/study/cookies">Cookies</a>
 <a href="/study/caching">Caching</a>
</div>


 </section>

</main>

<footer>
 <div class="footer-inner">
 <span>ITCode</span>
 <span>Programming & technology tutorials</span>
 </div>
</footer>

