<header><div class="header-inner">
<a href="#/index.html" class="logo"><span>IT</span>Code</a>
<nav><a href="#/index.html">Home</a><a href="/#programming">Programming</a><a href="/#networking">Networking</a><a href="/#other">Other</a></nav>
</div></header>
<main>
<div class="crumb"><a href="#/index.html">Home</a> &rsaquo; <a href="/#programming">Programming</a> &rsaquo; Python</div>
<article>
<h1>Python</h1>
<p class="lede">Python is readable, batteries-included, and everywhere &mdash; from quick scripts to data science. This is the core you need to start.</p>

<p>Python&rsquo;s whole design goal is readability. Blocks are defined by indentation rather than braces, and the standard library is enormous, so a lot of what you want to do is already written.</p>

<h2>Values and variables</h2>
<pre><code>name = "Ada" # str
age = 36 # int
height = 1.68 # float
is_admin = False # bool
items = ["a", "b"] # list
person = {"id": 1} # dict</code></pre>
<p>You do not declare types &mdash; a variable just points at a value, and can later point at a different one.</p>

<h2>Control flow</h2>
<pre><code>if age >= 18:
 print("adult")
elif age >= 13:
 print("teen")
else:
 print("child")

for item in items:
 print(item)

n = 0
while n < 3:
 n += 1</code></pre>
<p>The colon and the indentation are not optional &mdash; they <em>are</em> the block syntax.</p>

<h2>Functions</h2>
<pre><code>def greet(name, excited=False):
 msg = f"Hello, {name}"
 return msg + "!" if excited else msg

print(greet("Ada")) # Hello, Ada
print(greet("Ada", True)) # Hello, Ada!</code></pre>
<p>That <code>f"..."</code> is an <strong>f-string</strong> &mdash; the cleanest way to drop values into text.</p>

<h2>Collections you will use constantly</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>list</strong> &mdash; ordered, changeable: <code>nums = [3, 1, 2]; nums.sort()</code></li>
<li><strong>dict</strong> &mdash; key/value pairs: <code>user["name"]</code></li>
<li><strong>set</strong> &mdash; unique values: <code>set([1, 1, 2])</code> is <code>{1, 2}</code></li>
<li><strong>tuple</strong> &mdash; ordered, fixed: <code>point = (3, 4)</code></li>
</ul>

<h2>A list comprehension</h2>
<p>A Python idiom worth learning early &mdash; build a list in one expression:</p>
<pre><code>squares = [n * n for n in range(5)] # [0, 1, 4, 9, 16]
evens = [n for n in range(10) if n % 2 == 0]</code></pre>
<div class="note"><strong>Next step:</strong> once comfortable, look at modules (<code>import</code>), virtual environments (<code>python -m venv</code>), and <code>pip</code> for installing packages.</div>
</article>
<div class="more">
<h2>Keep reading</h2>
<div class="more-grid"><a href="#/study/javascript.html">JavaScript</a><a href="#/study/node.html">Node.js</a><a href="#/study/html.html">HTML &amp; CSS</a><a href="#/study/git.html">Git</a><a href="#/study/http.html">HTTP</a><a href="#/study/dns.html">DNS</a></div>
</div>
</main>
